I’ll inspect the measurement metadata, diffraction profile, and the supplied tungstate workflow/tooling first. Then I’ll identify candidate phases, build a multiphase GSAS-II refinement, and verify that every submitted artifact is generated from the saved `final.gpx`.

The sample chemistry is Mn–W–O from WO₃ + Mn₃O₄ fired at 800 °C. I’m now mapping the observed peak set against the frozen COD library and checking the local phase-search/GSAS-II interfaces; likely candidates include MnWO₄, residual oxides, and Mn-rich tungstates, but I’ll let the full profile distinguish them rather than assume the nominal product.

