The model remains stable in phase identity, lattice metrics, and quantitative fractions during these final profile cycles. I’ll stop once the improvement is below the practical significance of the count noise, then regenerate—not reuse—the calculated profile from the frozen project.

The profile is approaching a sensible physical limit: the common instrument width has stabilized, while WO₃’s uniaxial strain is converging toward the laboratory’s allowed anisotropy envelope. This behavior supports the anisotropic WO₃ profile term rather than an extra crystalline phase.

